# Git and Agent Rules

- Work from the current repository state; inspect before editing.
- Keep one coherent purpose per commit.
- Use imperative commit messages.
- Do not rewrite unrelated history.
- Do not modify generated/build artifacts unless they are explicitly versioned project outputs.
- Before completion, inspect the diff for unrelated changes and secrets.
- Report blockers instead of inventing undocumented requirements.
- For architecture changes, reference the relevant ADR in the implementation/PR description.
- Completion report must include changed files, build/test results, verification level and remaining risks.
